\title{sta310r: Data sets for the survival analysis course}
\description{
The \code{sta310r} package collects the data sets that accompany Collett (2023),
\emph{Modelling Survival Data in Medical Research} (4th edition), and the
computer exercises used in the STA310 course at the University of Gothenburg.
}
\section{Data sets}{

All 33 data sets distributed with the book are available with their original
column names and the short object names used in the course material (for
example \link{iud}, \link{breast}, \link{myeloma}, \link{ovarian}, \link{liver} and \link{rats}). Use
\code{data(package = "sta310r")} or the package index for a complete list. Each
data set is documented with the background of the study, the coded variables
and the relevant examples in Collett (2023).

In addition, \link{scottish_mbc_cohort} holds the synthetic Scottish metastatic
breast cancer cohort used in the computer exercise on survival analysis. It
does not come from the book and is documented with its own source.
}

\section{Computer exercises}{

The package ships the computer exercises as vignettes. Use
\code{vignette("cs1-survival-data")} for the questions and
\code{vignette("cs1-solutions")} for the same document with the solutions.
}

\references{
Collett, D. (2023) \emph{Modelling Survival Data in Medical Research}, 4th ed.
Chapman & Hall/CRC.
